From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:45:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/44] minimize: tab counts stay with the window while its
 title changes

Windows are matched to their tab counts by title, and the title often
changes before the source is rewritten: Claude Code animates the terminal
title about once a second, and switching a Firefox tab changes the title up
to 15 s before the session file catches up. Each miss dropped the second
row until the source caught up, so it flickered.

Each window now keeps the last count matched under its title and shows it
while its current title matches nothing. A real change of the count is
written under the then-current title and replaces it. The memory is
dropped when the window closes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BLrpLk9FRLLBEsz36L16sW

